{"path":"memory/allocator_traits/construct","title":"std::allocator_traits<Alloc>::construct","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::allocator_traits&lt;Alloc&gt;::</span>construct","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits/construct","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"If possible, constructs an object of type T in allocated uninitialized storage pointed to by p, by calling a.construct(p, std::forward<Args>(args)...).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/memory\">&lt;memory&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span>... <span class=\"me1\">Args</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> construct<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Alloc<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> a, T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p, Args<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>... <span class=\"me1\">args</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(constexpr since C++20)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>If possible, constructs an object of type <code>T</code> in allocated uninitialized storage pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code>, by calling\n<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a.<span class=\"me1\">construct</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Args<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>If the above is not possible (e.g. <code>Alloc</code> does not have the member function <code>construct()</code>), then calls\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-until-cxx20\"><td>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">new</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw1\">static_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> T<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Args<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-cxx20\"><td>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/construct_at\"><span class=\"kw3227\">std::<span class=\"me2\">construct_at</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Args<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> a\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> allocator to use for construction\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the uninitialized storage on which a <code>T</code> object will be constructed\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> args...\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the constructor arguments to pass to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a.<span class=\"me1\">construct</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> or to <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-until-cxx20\"><span>placement-new</span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></span></span><span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx20\"><span><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/construct_at\">std::construct_at()</a></span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span></span></span>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function is used by the standard library containers when inserting, copying, or moving elements.\n</p><p>Because this function provides the automatic fall back to placement new, the member function <code>construct()</code> is an optional <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Allocator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Allocator</em></a> requirement since C++11.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/operator_new\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator new</span><span>operator new[]</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocation functions <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator/construct\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>construct</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs an object in allocated storage <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::allocator&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/construct_at\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>construct_at</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  creates an object at a given address <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/allocator_traits","title":"std::allocator_traits"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::allocator_traits<Alloc>::construct","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. If possible, constructs an object of type T in allocated uninitialized storage pointed to by p, by calling…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"a, p, args..."},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function is used by the standard library containers when inserting, copying, or moving elements."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator new, operator new[]","note":"allocation functions"},{"label":"construct","note":"constructs an object in allocated storage"},{"label":"construct_at","note":"creates an object at a given address"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":179,"codeBlockCount":0}
